v",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Outlook it expresses"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"neutral-to-bearish"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Opens with"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"a credit"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Best case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"The premium received"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Worst case"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Unlimited above the strike"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Breakeven"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"Strike plus premium received"}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"flex gap-2","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"w-36 shrink-0 text-faint","children":"Exposures"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-text","children":"delta negative · gamma negative · theta positive · vega negative"}]]}]]}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"rounded-card border px-[18px] py-4 transition-colors duration-panel ease-standard bg-card border-border shadow-card","children":[["$","div",null,{"className":"mb-3 flex items-center gap-2","children":["$undefined",["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-base font-semibold leading-tight","children":["Lesson",false]}],false]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"text-[12.5px] leading-relaxed text-muted [&_h1]:mb-2 [&_h1]:text-base [&_h1]:font-bold [&_h1]:text-text [&_h2]:mb-1.5 [&_h2]:mt-5 [&_h2]:text-[13px] [&_h2]:font-bold [&_h2]:text-text [&_h3]:mb-1 [&_h3]:mt-4 [&_h3]:text-[12px] [&_h3]:font-semibold [&_h3]:text-text [&_p]:mb-2.5 [&_strong]:font-semibold [&_strong]:text-text [&_ul]:mb-2.5 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-5 [&_ol]:mb-2.5 [&_ol]:list-decimal [&_ol]:pl-5 [&_li]:mb-1 [&_code]:rounded [&_code]:bg-bg [&_code]:px-1 [&_code]:py-0.5 [&_code]:font-mono [&_code]:text-[11px] [&_code]:text-text [&_table]:mb-3 [&_table]:w-full [&_table]:text-left [&_table]:text-[11.5px] [&_th]:border-b [&_th]:border-border [&_th]:pb-1 [&_th]:pr-3 [&_th]:font-semibold [&_th]:text-text [&_td]:border-b [&_td]:border-border [&_td]:py-1 [&_td]:pr-3 [&_td]:align-top [&_a]:text-teal hover:[&_a]:underline [&_blockquote]:border-l-2 [&_blockquote]:border-border2 [&_blockquote]:pl-3 [&_blockquote]:italic","children":[["$","h1","h1-0",{"children":"Short Call"}],"\n",["$","p","p-0",{"children":"A naked short call is one sold call with no offsetting long position. It is the\r\nstructure with the least bounded risk profile available to a retail\r\nparticipant, and it is presented here because understanding it is a\r\nprerequisite for understanding every spread built on top of it — not because\r\nthe risk profile is comparable to the others in this section."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-0",{"children":"The structure"}],"\n",["$","p","p-1",{"children":"One leg: a short call, typically out of the money. Premium is credited at entry.\r\nMargin is blocked and marked to market daily."}],"\n",["$","p","p-2",{"children":"Unlike a long option, where the maximum loss is known at entry and already\r\npaid, a short call's obligation grows with the underlying. There is no upper\r\nbound on how far an index or a stock can rise."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-1",{"children":"What it is exposed to"}],"\n",["$","p","p-3",{"children":"Every greek reverses relative to a long call."}],"\n",["$","p","p-4",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Delta"}]," is negative — the position loses as the underlying rises."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-5",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gamma"}]," is negative, and this is the defining hazard. Negative gamma means\r\nthe position's delta worsens as the underlying moves against it: the higher the\r\nunderlying goes, the faster the position loses per additional point. Gamma\r\nmagnitude peaks at the money and rises steeply into expiry, so a short call\r\nthat is comfortably out of the money on Friday can be the dominant risk in an\r\naccount by Tuesday afternoon."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-6",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Theta"}]," is positive. This is the source of return — extrinsic value decays\r\ninto the seller's favour each day."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-7",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Vega"}]," is negative. A rise in implied volatility increases the option's value\r\nand therefore the loss, independently of direction."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-2",{"children":"Payoff"}],"\n",["$","p","p-8",{"children":"At expiry, anywhere at or below the strike, the call expires worthless and the\r\nfull premium is retained. Above the strike, loss accrues one-for-one with the\r\nunderlying, offset by the premium received. Breakeven is strike plus premium."}],"\n",["$","p","p-9",{"children":["The distribution of outcomes is the point: a high probability of a small gain,\r\nagainst a low probability of a loss with no defined ceiling. Expectancy is not\r\ndetermined by win rate. See ",["$","code","code-0",{"children":"risk/expectancy.md"}],"."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-3",{"children":"Indian market specifics"}],"\n",["$","p","p-10",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Margin."}]," SPAN plus exposure margin is blocked at entry and recomputed\r\nthrough the day. SEBI moved position-limit monitoring to multiple intraday\r\nsnapshots from April 2025, so intraday breaches are now caught rather than\r\nnetted out by close."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-11",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Expiry-day margin."}]," An additional 2% extreme loss margin applies to short\r\noption positions on expiry day, in force since November 2024. Separately, the\r\ncalendar-spread margin benefit was withdrawn on expiry day from February 2025 —\r\na short call that was margin-offset by a longer-dated leg loses that offset on\r\nthe day it matters most."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-12",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"STT."}]," 0.15% of premium on the sale. If assigned, the exercise-side STT of\r\n0.15% of intrinsic value applies to the counterparty, not the writer."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-13",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Physical settlement."}]," A short stock call finishing in the money obliges\r\ndelivery of shares on E+2. A writer without the stock must buy it, at whatever\r\nprice the market offers, on a compressed timeline. Delivery margins begin four\r\ntrading days before expiry. This is a materially different risk from an index\r\nshort call, which is cash settled."]}],"\n",["$","p","p-14",{"children":[["$","strong","strong-0",{"children":"Gap risk."}]," Indian equities and indices can gap on overnight global cues,\r\npolicy announcements and results. A short call carries the gap in full: there\r\nis no stop-loss that executes between the previous close and the opening\r\nprint."]}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-4",{"children":"How it typically fails"}],"\n",["$","p","p-15",{"children":"The characteristic loss is not gradual. A short call sold far out of the money\r\nprints many small gains, which raises confidence and usually position size, and\r\nthe loss when it arrives arrives at a size calibrated to the enlarged position\r\nrather than the original one. Negative gamma is what converts a modest adverse\r\nmove into a disproportionate loss late in the contract's life."}],"\n",["$","h2","h2-5",{"children":"Related"}],"\n",["$","ul","ul-0",{"children":["\n",["$","li","li-0",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/directional/covered-call.md"}]," — the same leg with stock held\r\nagainst it, which bounds the upside loss"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-1",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"strategies/vertical-spreads/bear-call-spread.md"}]," — the same leg with a\r\nfurther call bought above it, which caps the loss at the spread width"]}],"\n",["$","li","li-2",{"children":[["$","code","code-0",{"children":"greeks/gamma.md"}]," — why the risk accelerates rather than accrues"]}],"\n"]}]]}]]}],["$","p",null,{"className":"text-[10px] leading-relaxed text-faint","children":["Educational material describing how a structure behaves. Not a recommendation, not a signal, and not personalised advice. Source: ",["$","code",null,{"className":"font-mono","children":"docs/learning/strategies/directional/short-call.md"}]]}]]}],null],null],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children","$4","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children","strategy","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[null,["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children","learning","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":"$undefined","template":["$","$L5",null,{}],"templateStyles":"$undefined","templateScripts":"$undefined","notFound":"$undefined","notFoundStyles":"$undefined"}]],null]},[[null,["$","$L6",null,{"children":["$","$L3",null,{"parallelRouterKey":"children","segmentPath":["children","(workspace)","children"],"error":"$undefined","errorStyles":"$undefined","errorScripts":